      "source_number": "223",
      "independent_solution": "Compute every adjacent difference in each finite list as written. (a) 17-7=10, 27-17=10, 37-27=10: arithmetic progression, d=10. (b) The literal list is -17,-7,7,17,27, including positive 7. Its differences are 10,14,10,10: not an arithmetic progression. Do not change the 7 to 3 or insert an absent term. (c) 12-2=10, 22-12=10, 32-22=10: arithmetic progression, d=10. (d) 22-2=20 and 222-22=200: not an arithmetic progression. (e) Consecutive differences are 3/4-1/4=1/2, 5/4-3/4=1/2, 7/4-5/4=1/2: arithmetic progression, d=1/2. (f) 4/5-4/3=-8/15, 4/7-4/5=-8/35, 4/9-4/7=-8/63: not an arithmetic progression. Equal denominator increments do not imply equal differences of the fractions. The complete classification in a-f order is yes, no, yes, no, yes, no.",
