    {
      "source_number": "231",
      "independent_solution": "Both parts are exponent-law evaluation tasks, not arithmetic-progression tasks; a and b are nonzero under the given substitutions. (a) 4a^3 b^(-5) * 2a^(-4)b^4 = 8a^(3-4)b^(-5+4) = 8a^(-1)b^(-1) = 8/(ab). Here a=6.4*10^3=6400 and b=2.5*10^(-2)=0.025=1/40, so ab=160 and the value is 8/160=1/20=0.05=5*10^(-2). Equivalently ab=(6.4*2.5)*10^(3-2)=16*10=160. (b) (3^(-1)a^(-1)b^2)^2 = 3^(-2)a^(-2)b^4 = (1/9)a^(-2)b^4. Multiplication by 9a^3b^(-5) cancels the coefficient and gives a^(-2+3)b^(4-5)=a/b. With a=3.7*10^2=370 and b=1.7*10^(-1)=0.17=17/100, the value is 37000/17 = (37/17)*10^3, approximately 2176.470588235294. The exact fraction is required unless a rounding convention is explicitly supplied; the source supplies none. A simplified symbolic expression alone is not the requested numerical evaluation.",
      "task_requirements": [
        "Evaluate both complete expressions at their distinct stated a and b values.",
        "Apply product and power rules correctly, including squaring every factor in the parenthesized product in part (b).",
        "Distinguish negative exponents from negative numbers and preserve the nonzero-base condition.",
        "In part (a), retain coefficient 8 and simplify to 8/(ab), then compute the numeric value 1/20.",
        "In part (b), square 3^(-1) to 3^(-2), cancel against 9, simplify to a/b and compute the exact value 37000/17.",
        "Preserve scientific-notation exponents and do not silently impose an unspecified rounding precision.",
        "Keep this source's exponent/evaluation task distinct from the progression tasks in 223-230."
      ],
      "required_response_units": [
